# tuneshine-info -- example crontab
#
# Pushes a clock + weather frame to every Tuneshine on the LAN, once a minute,
# whenever a device is idle.
#
# Install:
#   crontab -e
# and paste the line at the bottom, editing the path.
#   -- or --
#   crontab crontab.example
#
# Notes:
#   * Use an absolute python path. cron's PATH is minimal and often has no
#     `python3`.
#   * The machine running this must be online. It is the thing that pushes to
#     the device, so nothing updates while it is off.
#   * stdout and stderr are discarded here. The script prints only on a new
#     failure and on recovery, and always writes a line to
#     <state_dir>/tuneshine_info.log.
#   * Check your config first with an absolute path to be safe:
#     /usr/bin/python3 /opt/tuneshine-info/tuneshine_info.py --preview

* * * * * /usr/bin/python3 /opt/tuneshine-info/tuneshine_info.py >/dev/null 2>&1
